 - **12 virtual gates**, six per development sequence. They are image-space geometries defined by the frozen GT height relation, not real-world calibrated ground-plane exits.
 - The whole-sequence population contains **901 transitions: 724 rule-confirmed and 177 unconfirmed**. MOT20-01 contributes 90/74 transitions/confirmed, MOT20-02 contributes 811/650. The older core-window population is smaller (837/671); it is retained as metadata but is **not** the denominator of this sample's E1 v2 main score.
-- A valid body-box bottom-centre point changing from one non-gap region to the other produces a transition. Its timestamp is the first observed target-region entry. This is not an interpolated physical instant at the centre line.
+- A valid body-box bottom-centre point changing from one non-gap region to the other produces a transition. Its timestamp is the first observed target-region entry. The recorded position is the reference point at that entry frame, not a projection onto the centre line; C1 confirmation does not redefine it. The extractor does not test intersection with the finite centre-line segment. Points outside both regions are treated as gap, so a region transition must not be equated without qualification with a physical crossing of that finite segment.
 - The included example uses existing **YOLOX-X + v11 downstream** outputs. Identity association is rebuilt using the actual output trajectory boxes, not all detector input boxes. The sample does not rerun tracking or the C1/R1/R2 event decoder.
 - Main event matching requires the same GT person, the same direction, time difference at most 1 second, and native-image distance at most the frozen GT body height. Matching first maximizes cardinality, then minimizes total absolute time difference, then resolves ties deterministically.
